    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0701" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg599"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/161: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-14T19:00:00+01:00">February 14,
                            1935—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 14—3:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. My 69, February 13, noon.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d473-f1"/> Recent information
                    all points to a more general preparation for an extensive campaign in Abyssinia
                    than was indicated by the announcements of the Italian Government. Military
                    forces and supplies are being moved clandestinely. Every effort is being made to
                    prevent information of the size or general nature of the shipments. Troops
                    called are kept in barracks and denied freedom. Movements are by night.</p>
                <p>I am today advised by a person I believe well informed that 30,000 troops have
                    left the port of Naples; that the movement now under way contemplates between
                    200,000 and 300,000 troops being used in Ethiopia; and that the troops who are
                    now or who have been recently in Tripoli and thus have had tropical experience
                    are being transferred to the Ethiopian front and are being replaced by forces
                    from Italy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
